      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX.2 [klein]: img2img, references\n\n[FLUX.2 [klein]](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-9b-fp8) (Black Forest Labs, 9B, Qwen3 8B text\nencoder) is a fast step-distilled text-to-image and multi-reference editing model, set up here with every Generate\ntab feature that ComfyUI offers for it. Write full descriptive sentences and put literal text in quotes.\n\n**Settings (distilled, this workflow)**: 4 steps, CFG 1, euler, `Flux2Scheduler`, 1024×1024 (multiples of 16).\nThe negative conditioning is zeroed (**ConditioningZeroOut**): at CFG 1 there is no negative pass, so the Generate tab\nshows no negative prompt. Raising CFG burns the image.\n\n**Base** (`flux-2-klein-base-9b-fp8`, undistilled, for LoRA training or true CFG): pick it in the model list, set 20-30\nsteps and CFG about 4. For a negative prompt, replace **ConditioningZeroOut** with a **CLIP Text Encode** titled\n`ib:np`, fed by the clip output of the Image Bench Prompt and passed through Reference Latent nodes of its own if\nyou use references.\n\n**klein 4B** (Apache-2.0): `flux-2-klein-4b-fp8` with the `qwen_3_4b` text encoder in **Load CLIP**, same settings.\nLoRAs and ControlNets of FLUX.2 [dev] do not load on klein (a different transformer).\n\n## img2img\n\nThe image of **Load Image ib:img** is the starting point: **Resize to** scales it to the size of the Generate tab\n(Width / Height, its *Resize to* in img2img mode; **Use size** in the Input cell takes the size of the image),\n**VAE Encode** makes the latent, and the sampler adds noise by the **denoising** strength (0.6 here) and samples\nfrom there. The prompt describes the whole image you want. Low denoising keeps the composition and colors; high\ndenoising moves further from the image. To change one area only, use the inpaint workflow; to change the image by\nan instruction, an edit model with references.\n\nThe Generate tab is in **img2img** mode while this workflow is loaded. Send an image with **Send to the input\nimage** (B), from the editor, or upload it in the Input cell before the first queue. This workflow has no Hires.\nfix pass: upscale the result with the full workflow.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:img` | Load Image | Input cell; Send to the input image (B), the editor |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | SamplerCustomAdvanced | seed (RandomNoise), steps (Flux2Scheduler), sampling method, CFG scale (CFGGuider), denoising; Resize to (Width / Height) |\n| `ib:ref:0-3` | Reference 1-4 (bypassed) | References panel |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**References** (up to 4; klein takes up to 10, add slots by copying a column and numbering its loader\n`ib:ref:4`, ...): add images in the References panel of the Generate tab (a tab next to LoRA), by \"Ps sends to:\nreference\" from Photoshop, or by dropping them there. An empty slot is bypassed together with its scale and encode\nnodes; its **Reference Latent** stays and passes the conditioning on unchanged. Refer to the references by order in\nthe prompt (*\"the woman from image 1 wearing the jacket from image 2\"*); for an edit, say what changes and what stays\n(*\"change the jacket to red leather, keep the face, pose and background\"*). Each is scaled to 1 MP first. The zeroed\nnegative keeps the references, so they also act in the negative pass of the base model.\n\nPut any ESRGAN-type model into\n`models/upscale_models` ([RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Real-ESRGAN_repackaged/resolve/main/RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors) here).\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt; the **Image Bench Prompt** node\napplies them. **Load LoRA** stays bypassed; LoRA exploration enables it for its runs and bypasses it again.\n\nBatch generation, model and LoRA exploration, varying parameters, PNG Info, projects and the Compare tab work\nas with every marked workflow. The ControlNet tab has no units here: ComfyUI has no ControlNet for klein; use a pose\nor depth map as a reference instead (*\"in the pose of image 2\"*).\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [flux-2-klein-9b-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-9b-fp8/resolve/main/flux-2-klein-9b-fp8.safetensors) (distilled), [flux-2-klein-base-9b-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-9b-fp8/resolve/main/flux-2-klein-base-9b-fp8.safetensors) (base)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein-9B/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors)\n**vae**: [full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-small-decoder/resolve/main/full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors)\n\nFLUX.2 [klein] 9B is released under the FLUX Non-Commercial License, klein 4B under Apache-2.0.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: FLUX.2 [klein] (Image Bench, img2img)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
